 ('law_copy_commanded', 'status', "the copy of the law commanded — the STATUS the line king_law_declared writes on Israel: 'and when he sits on the throne of his kingdom, HE SHALL WRITE FOR HIMSELF A COPY OF THIS LAW ON A BOOK from before the priests the Levites; and it shall be with him and he shall read in it all the days of his life' (17:18-19) — worthy of the throne when he does all (the Sifrei 160:1); for his own name, never his fathers' (160:2); the whole Torah, the book's name for the change of script and the assembly's reading (160:3-4); on a scroll, not a tablet nor paper, of a clean beast's skin, CORRECTED FROM THE COURTYARD'S SCROLL BY THE SEVENTY-ONE (160:5-7); R. Elazar ben Arakh's prophecy of forgetting (160:8); with him going out, coming in, in judgment and at table (161:1 — Mishnah Sanhedrin 2:4), the nights too by 'all' (161:2 — Berakhot 1:5's move); the king's own ledger a FUTURE entity's", H['copy'] + " (and he shall write for himself a copy of this law on a book — Deut 17:18)", "Deut 17:18-19, 31:9-13 (the assembly's reading, ahead), 31:26; Onkelos 17:18-19 ('the scroll'); the Sifrei on Deuteronomy 160:1-8, 161:1-2; Mishnah Sanhedrin 2:4 (the exam — read whole); Tosefta Sanhedrin 4:7 (by the English's note — owed)", CORPUS, EX % ("F4 the_king — the_copy_of_the_law", "king_law_declared")),
