 ('first_fleece_owed', 'status', "the first of the fleece owed — the STATUS the line priests_dues_declared writes on Israel: 'THE FIRST OF YOUR GRAIN, YOUR WINE AND YOUR OIL, AND THE FIRST OF THE FLEECE OF YOUR FLOCK YOU SHALL GIVE HIM' (18:4) — only from the choicest, kind for kind (the Sifrei 166:1 — the grain, wine and oil Numbers 18:12's grant by CALL to korach); the fleece not the washed-off, not the torn, everywhere (166:2-4); 'your flock' and not others' — the gentile's flock exempt, the seller who kept some liable else the buyer (166:5 — Mishnah Chullin 11:2 cited in the spine's Hebrew); 'you shall give him' enough for a gift — five selas in Judea, ten in Galilee, whitened not dyed, enough for a small garment (166:6 — 'ibid.'); TWO EWES (Shammai — Isaiah 7:21) OR FIVE (Hillel — 1 Samuel 25:18; 166:7-8); R. AKIVA'S FIVE counted out of the verse's own words (166:9): the threshold and the measure PARAMETERS with both houses' arms", H['fleece'] + " (and the first of the fleece of your flock you shall give him — Deut 18:4)", "Deut 18:4; Numbers 18:12 (korach by CALL — the best of the oil, wine and grain); Isaiah 7:21, 1 Samuel 25:18 (the houses' grounds — the Prophets' tape ahead); Onkelos 18:4; the Sifrei on Deuteronomy 166:1-9; Mishnah Chullin 11:1-2 (the exam — read whole)", CORPUS, EX % ("F5 the_priests_dues — the_first_fruits_and_the_fleece", "priests_dues_declared")),
